# Content frame

On the website, important information and supporting graphics do not share an edge.

Titles, text, controls, and the frames that carry the work sit inside one content frame. On the 1920 × 560 classroom sheet that frame ends 60px from the right edge (`--home-content-right` in `app/globals.css`). The left edge is the rail clearance, so the open menu names stay clear of the information.

Supporting graphics may bleed past the frame to the sheet edge, including under the left rail. Home and Studio are the model: the field runs to the edge, and the text, plates, and frames stay inside the 60px line.

Do not give a new page its own right inset. Use `--home-content-right`. A graphic that should bleed opts into the sheet edge. It does not move the information frame.

This is the website frame. It does not restyle the internal lab panels.
